{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;\r\nmso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;\r\nmso-font-kerning:0pt;mso-ansi-language:EN-GB;mso-fareast-language:EN-GB;\r\nmso-bidi-language:AR-SA&quot;&gt;The proposed extension would introduce a permanent\r\nfeature that would be out of character and appearance with the parade of shops\r\nwithin the locality. The front elevation of the parade is\r\ncharacterised by a uniform line and so a permanent structure would become\r\noverly stark and dominant, to the detriment of the character and appearance of\r\nthe street scene and the visual amenities of the area. The proposal is therefore\r\ncontrary to the high quality design aspirations of the National Planning Policy\r\nFramework (2023), Policy D3.D.1 and D.11 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy\r\nCS1.B of the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), Policy DM1 and DM4 of the Harrow\r\nDevelopment Management Policies Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
